<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.11.6: Graphing Using Transformations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01059</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.11.6: Graphing Using Transformations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>fd775b0d-eaf8-4961-bf13-fe0f9d817f22</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">For questions 1 - 4, match each equation of the linear functions with one of the lines in the given graph.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Match each equation of the linear functions with one of the lines in the given graph.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">
          <media alt="Graph of four functions where the orange line has a \(y\)-intercepts at 3 and slope of 2, the baby blue line has a \(y\)-intercepts at 3 and slope of 1/2, the blue line has a \(y\)-intercepts at 3 and slope of -2, and the green line has a \(y\)-intercepts at -3 and slope of 2.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_14_15_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">\(f(x)=2x+3\)</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00006">I</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">\(g(x)=2x−3\)</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00009">III</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">\(h(x)=−2x+3\)</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00011">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00012">IV</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00013">\(j(x)=\frac{1}{2}x+3\)</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00014">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00015">II</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section id="sect-00002">
        <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
        <exercise id="_5f4f2259-2fef-4583-987d-86e9687e8b43" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00016">How will the graph of k(x) = x be affected if the transformation k(x - 3) is applied?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00017">Correct! The graph will be shifted 3 units to the right. This happens because the transformation \(k(x-3)\) moves the graph horizontally to the right by 3 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00018">Try again. Think about how subtracting from the variable inside the function affects the graph’s position on the horizontal axis.</para>
            <para id="para-00019">The correct answer is: The graph will be shifted 3 units to the right. By applying the transformation \(k(x - 3)\), the graph is moved 3 units to the right, which shifts each point on the graph horizontally.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content></document>